---
source: crates/cli/tests/native.rs
expression: run.stdout
---
Compare two files line by line, as GNU diff does

Usage: tw diff [OPTIONS] [FILE]...

Arguments:
  [FILE]...  The two files; - for stdin

Options:
  -u                            Unified format, 3 lines of context
  -U, --unified [<NUM>]         Unified format with NUM lines of context (3 when not given)
      --label <LABEL>           Name a file LABEL in the unified header; twice for both
  -q, --brief                   Say only whether the files differ
  -s, --report-identical-files  Say so when the files are the same
  -i, --ignore-case             Lines that differ in case only are the same
  -w, --ignore-all-space        White space is not compared at all
  -b, --ignore-space-change     Runs of white space are one space, and trailing white space is none
  -h, --help                    Print help
